={{
  {
    "model": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile",
    "response_format": { "type": "json_object" },
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "system",
        "content": "You are a master content strategist writing on behalf of a Chief AI Officer at an AI startup. Write with high-level authority, technical precision (e.g., Andrej Karpathy, not Carpa), and zero marketing fluff.

*** MANDATORY RULE: Your response must be in JSON format. ***

CRITICAL FORMATTING INSTRUCTIONS:
1. The 'linkedin_text' field must NOT use Markdown bolding (no **asterisks**).
2. You MUST use DOUBLE LINE BREAKS between paragraphs to ensure readability on LinkedIn.
3. Use simple bullet points (•).
4. Spell names and concepts correctly.

Desired Structure Example (FOLLOW THIS EXACTLY):

[Punchy hook line about the problem/solution].

[Context line describing what you did].

[Outcome statement].

• Point 1 about how you did it.

[CTA/Closing statement].

#[hashtag] #[hashtag]

Output only a JSON object with this schema:
{
  "linkedin_text": "The FULL post text without markdown bolding, using DOUBLE line breaks between EVERY paragraph.",
  "image_prompt": "Prompt for Flux.ai / DALL-E 3 description",
  "full_telegram_message": "Valid HTML message for Telegram (using <b>, <code> tags)"
}"
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "RAW VOICE TRANSCRIPT / IDEA:
" + ($json.text || $json.message?.text || "")
      }
    ]
  }
}}

parameters.jsCode:
let rawContent = $input.first().json.choices[0].message.content;

// No longer need regex cleanup because we enforced json_object format.
// Just parse the clean string.

try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(rawContent);

  // Basic sanity check on the expected keys
  if (!parsed.linkedin_text || !parsed.full_telegram_message) {
    throw new Error("Parsed JSON is missing critical keys.");
  }

  return [{
    json: {
      linkedin_text: parsed.linkedin_text.trim(),
      image_prompt: parsed.image_prompt || "",
      full_telegram_message: parsed.full_telegram_message.trim()
    }
  }];
} catch (e) {
  // If parsing fails, we output a structure that downstream 
  // nodes can't easily use for posting.
  return [{
    json: {
      linkedin_text: "", // Prevents posting to LinkedIn
      image_prompt: "",
      full_telegram_message: `⚠️ <b>JSON Error</b>\\\\nUnable to parse the LLM output. View Raw Output: \\\\n\\\\n<code>${rawContent}</code>`
    }
  }];
}
